    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Mississauga-Assistant-Professor%2C-Teaching-Stream-Macroeconomics-ON/605576017/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Teaching Stream",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Teaching Stream - Macroeconomics Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Assistant Professor, Teaching Stream - Macroeconomics Date Posted: 08/26/2026 Closing Date: 11/16/2026, 11:59PM ET Req ID: 48811 Job Category: Faculty - Teaching Stream (continuing) Faculty/Division: University of Toronto Mississauga (UTM) Department: UTM: Economics Campus: University of Toronto Mississauga (UTM) Existing Vacancy: Yes POSITION DESCRIPTION The Department of Economics at the University of Toronto Mississauga (UTM) invites applications for a full-time teaching stream position in macroeconomics. The appointment will be at the rank of Assistant Professor, Teaching Stream with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. We seek enthusiastic and innovative individuals pursuing a successful and impactful career in university teaching, with both the demonstrated ability and capacity to enhance the domestic and international reputation of our undergraduate programs. REQUIREMENTS AND QUALIFICATIONS Applicants must have earned a PhD degree in Economics by the time of appointment, or shortly thereafter, specializing in macroeconomics or a related field, with a demonstrated record of excellence in teaching. We seek candidates whose teaching interests complement and enhance our existing departmental strengths. The successful candidate must present clear evidence of: excellence in teaching in a degree-granting program, including lecture preparation and delivery, curriculum development, and design of high-quality course materials and assessments; a demonstrated commitment to excellent pedagogical practices and continued professional development; a demonstrated commitment to the scholarship of teaching and learning and to educational leadership; good judgement and a reflective approach to teaching innovation; excellent expository, organizational, and interpersonal skills, including the ability to collaborate effectively with colleagues on our courses and programs; and the demonstrated capacity to expertly incorporate current research into our undergraduate courses. Evidence of the above criteria requires: a creative and coherent teaching dossier that highlights teaching accomplishments, including a thoughtful and compelling teaching statement, sample syllabi and course materials, and teaching evaluations; publications and/or working papers in macroeconomics or a related field; and strong letters of reference from referees of high standing. Evidence may also include professional experiences that enhance teaching, awards and accolades, presentations at significant conferences, or other evidence of superior performance in teaching-related activities submitted as part of the application.  The candidate’s teaching dossier, papers, and letters of reference should give evidence of excellent expository, organizational, and interpersonal skills and the requisite expertise in macroeconomics. RESPONSIBILITIES Teaching duties are focused on macroeconomics courses in the undergraduate programs of the Department of Economics at the University of Toronto Mississauga. These courses may include program-required courses at the first and/or second year level, as well as upper-year undergraduate courses. In addition, the successful candidate is expected to contribute to the broader Economics community at the University of Toronto through service and administrative activities, and through active participation in teaching and learning workshops, conferences, and mentoring. HIRING SALARY RANGE The salary range is CAD 155,000 – 185,000 per annum, depending on experience. Negotiations beyond this salary range will be considered for exceptionally qualified candidates. ABOUT US Information about the Department of Economics at the University of Toronto Mississauga is available at https://www.utm.utoronto.ca/economics/ and information about the broader Economics community at the University of Toronto is available at https://www.economics.utoronto.ca/ . For more information on working at the University of Toronto, please visit https://www.utoronto.ca/research-innovation/working-at-uoft . At UTM we are committed to fostering an environment of diversity and inclusion. With an enviably diverse student body, we especially welcome applications from candidates who identify as Indigenous, Black, or racially visible (persons of colour), and who have experience working with, teaching or mentoring diverse groups or students. Candidates must demonstrate, in their application materials, an ability to foster diversity on campus and within the curriculum or discipline, and must show evidence of a commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, and the promotion of a respectful and collegial environment. Candidates must submit a statement describing their contributions to equity, diversity, and inclusion (EDI), which might cover topics such as (but not limited to): teaching that incorporates a focus on underrepresented communities; efforts undertaken to develop inclusive pedagogies, collaboration, and engagement with underrepresented communities; and mentoring of students from underrepresented groups. If you have questions about this statement, please contact drew.reid@utoronto.ca . APPLICATION PROCESS Applications must be submitted online at https://econjobmarket.org/ . Applicants must submit the following materials: a cover letter; a current curriculum vitae; a complete teaching dossier, including a teaching statement, sample syllabi and select course materials that directly support and illustrate the teaching statement, and teaching evaluations or evidence of superior performance in other teaching-related activities as listed above; a job market paper and up to three working papers or publications; an EDI statement (as outlined above); and the name and contact information of at least three references. At least one reference letter must primarily address the candidate’s teaching. EconJobMarket will automatically solicit and collect letters of reference from each referee once an application is submitted. Applicants, however, remain responsible for ensuring that references submit recent letters (on letterhead, dated and signed) by the closing date. Review of applications will begin on November 16, 2026 and applicants should endeavour to have all materials including reference letters submitted by then; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Only complete applications will be considered. If you have any questions about this position, please contact drew.reid@utoronto.ca . Caution: This ad is “posted only” to the U of T faculty job board. Please see the information above for the application instructions. Applications submitted via the U of T platform will NOT be considered for this position. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Curriculum Development, Teacher, Academic, Equity, Education, Research, Finance Apply now » Find similar jobs: Faculty Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
    },
    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Risk-and-Resilience-Specialist-ON/606437817/": {
      "title": "Risk and Resilience Specialist",
      "description": "Risk and Resilience Specialist Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Risk and Resilience Specialist Date Posted: 09/24/2026 Req ID: 50306 Faculty/Division: VP Legal, Risk & Safety Department: Office of Enterprise Risk Management & Insurance Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The Risk and Resilience Specialist plays a key role in the continued development, implementation and administration of the University’s Enterprise Risk Management, Insurance, and Business Continuity programs. The incumbent is responsible for independently managing the day-to-day delivery of the University’s enterprise risk management and business continuity programs and providing senior analytical and program support to the insurance portfolio. In this dynamic role, the Risk and Resilience Specialist is reporting to the Director, Enterprise Risk Management & Insurance. The role facilitates risk assessments; develops frameworks, tools and resources to support consistent risk management practices; and facilitates institution-wide business continuity and resilience activities. The Risk and Resilience Specialist is responsible for moving initiatives from concept through implementation, monitoring progress, identifying emerging issues and ensuring risk management activities remain aligned with institutional priorities. The role requires the ability to build relationships, influence without direct authority and translate complex risk information into practical recommendations. The Risk and Resilience Specialist works with the Director, Enterprise Risk Management & Insurance to develop and manage systems (and related protocols) to maintain timely, detailed, secure, and confidential case files and records, which adhere to all University retention and FIPPA policies. Qualifications Required: I. EDUCATION: University degree in business administration, risk management, finance, public administration, or another relevant discipline, or an acceptable combination of education and experience. II. EXPERIENCE: Minimum five (5) years of experience in enterprise risk management, business continuity, project management, or a related discipline, preferably within a university, public-sector, or similarly complex organization. Demonstrated experience leading complex initiatives involving multiple stakeholders and competing priorities. Experience maintaining databases, registers, trackers, records, and document-management systems. Experience conducting risk assessment and translating complex information into clear, practical recommendations. Demonstrated experience working effectively with individuals across multiple organizational levels. Experience collecting, reviewing, consolidating, and presenting information for reports, dashboards, briefing notes, or presentations. Experience leading multi-stakeholder projects is an asset. III. SKILLS: Excellent facilitation, consultation and stakeholder engagement skills. Strong written communication skills, including experience preparing professional correspondence, reports, meeting materials, and presentations. Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Office products, including and not limited to, Excel, PowerPoint, and Word. Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail. IV. OTHER: Demonstrated ability to independently plan, prioritize and execute complex work with limited supervision. Demonstrated ability to monitor multiple deliverables, manage competing priorities, and follow-up effectively on outstanding actions Ability to exercise sound judgement, discretion, diplomacy, and tact when working with sensitive and confidential information. Demonstrated initiative, resourcefulness, and ability to work both independently and collaboratively. Closing Date: 10/15/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 3 -- Hiring Zone: $93,592 - $109,190 -- Broadband Salary Range: $93,592  - $155,985 Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Risk Management, Document Management, Project Manager, Finance, Technology Apply now » Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
