    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-AssistantAssociate-or-Full-Professor-Division-of-Neurosurgery-ON/606482517/": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate or Full Professor",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate or Full Professor - Division of Neurosurgery Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Assistant/Associate or Full Professor - Division of Neurosurgery Date Posted: 09/25/2026 Closing Date: 10/30/2026 , 11:59PM ET Req ID: 50302 Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Surgery Hospital Affiliation: UHN - Toronto Western Hospital Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The Division of Neurosurgery in the Sprott Department of Surgery at the University Health Network (UHN), Princess Margaret Cancer Centre and the University of Toronto are accepting applications for a full-time Academic Neurosurgeon at the rank of Assistant/Associate or Full Professor, with a specific interest and demonstrated training and experience in skull base surgery and neuro-oncology. The individual we seek should have advanced training and skills in these areas through formal fellowship experience; completion of a fellowship in skull base surgery and neurosurgical oncology is mandatory. Depending on the successful candidate’s University of Toronto faculty status, the applicant may be eligible to apply for the Crean Hotson Chair in Skull Base Surgery. The effective date of this appointment will be July 1st 2027, but can be flexible depending on the candidate. The successful applicant will manage patients with complex intracranial and skull base pathology, including primary and metastatic brain tumours, pituitary and anterior/lateral/posterior skull base lesions, and other neuro-oncologic disease. The primary appointment of the individual will be in the Division of Neurosurgery at UHN, which offers an excellent opportunity for career development with an internationally recognized tradition of academic neurosurgery situated in a rich clinical and academic environment. The Division has a well-established subspecialty practice in skull base surgery and neuro-oncology, with a long-standing history of multidisciplinary care in the neuro-oncology program. The candidate should display interest and training in open and endoscopic skull base approaches and collaborative multidisciplinary neuro-oncology care. The candidate will be considered active staff, covering neurosurgical call; educating neurosurgery trainees, medical students, and other learners; promoting a positive work culture and supportive training environment; prioritizing patient-centred care; and striving for diversity within the community. Evidence of excellence in teaching and research is required. The successful candidate will be appointed either a surgeon-teacher, or surgeon-investigator, or surgeon-scientist and must demonstrate a strong record of teaching and research excellence, as appropriate. Applicants are required to hold an MD degree and certification in Neurosurgery from the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada, or a recognized equivalent certifying body. The candidate must have completed a residency program in Neurosurgery as well as a fellowship in Skull Base Surgery . A secondary graduate degree at the masters (MSc) or doctoral level (PhD) is required. The individual must be eligible for licensure by the College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario. All candidates must be proficient in English. Applicants should demonstrate a track record of commitment to excellence in neurosurgical training, clinical service, and scholarship, and seek a position that would involve a significant time commitment to academic activities focused on research. This position entails a full-time faculty appointment in the Department of Surgery at the University of Toronto. The candidate must be eligible for an appointment at the academic rank of Assistant/Associate or Full Professor. Remuneration will be derived from a variety of sources, primarily from, but not limited to, fee-for-service clinical billings, and commensurate with rank as a member of the Clinical Faculty, qualifications, and experience. Academic start-up funds or a research Chair will be provided in alignment with the credentials and experience of the candidate. Based on the expected clinical workload, the annual base compensation for this position is estimated to be $500,000. The specific amount will depend on the individual's clinical workload, ensuring that the compensation reflects the responsibilities undertaken. Applications will be accepted until October 30th, or until the position is filled. Interested individuals should send a copy of their letter of interest, curriculum vitae and the names of three referees by email to: Suneil K. Kalia MD PhD FAANS FCNS FRCSC Head of Division - Neurosurgery - Toronto Western Hospital and University Health Network (UHN) R.R. Tasker Chair in Stereotactic and Functional Neurosurgery Senior Scientist - Krembil Research Institute and KITE Associate Professor - University of Toronto West Wing 4-428, Toronto Western Hospital 399 Bathurst Street. Toronto, ON. M5T 2S8 phone: 416-603-5866 fax: 416-603-5298 email: suneil.kalia@uhn.ca For more information about the Temerty Faculty of Medicine/Department of Surgery and the Sprott Department of Surgery, University Health Network, please visit http://surgery.utoronto.ca and https://www.uhn.ca/Sprott-Surgery CAUTION: This ad is “posted only” to the U of T affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Neurology, Oncology, Pathology, Gastroenterology, Research Scientist, Healthcare, Science Apply now » Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
