      "title": "Faculty Relations Consultant Job Details",
      "description": "Faculty Relations Consultant Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Faculty Relations Consultant Date Posted: 09/28/2026 Req ID: 50340 Faculty/Division: Vice-President & Provost Department: Office of the Vice- Provost, Faculty & Academic Life Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About Us The Office of the Vice-Provost, Faculty & Academic Life (VPFAL) is the institutional office responsible for providing academic human resources services in relation to faculty members and librarians across the University. It provides advice, support, and/or approval to Divisions and divisional academic human resources teams and the senior administration on a broad range of matters related to the academic life cycle. The office also serves as the primary point of contact for engagement with the University of Toronto Faculty Association, including in relation to salary, benefit and workload negotiations, investigations, policy revision and development, as well as grievances and arbitration. Your Opportunity Under the general direction of the Associate Director, and working in collaboration with a wide range of offices both internal and external to the University, the Faculty Relations Consultant will provide a broad range of support in respect of academic human resources and faculty/labour relations activities across the University of Toronto, with a primary focus on negotiations with the UTFA and case management of grievances and workplace complaints involving faculty members and librarians. These include complaints regarding alleged incidents of bullying, harassment, discrimination, sexual violence, and complaints from students regarding their experience with graduate supervision.  The incumbent will also provide support on related governance processes (i.e., bringing matters through Governing Council processes for information or approval). The role requires strong skills and knowledge in employee and labour relations, issue assessment, case management, stakeholder consultation, conflict resolution, policy interpretation, collective agreement administration, and handling highly sensitive and confidential workplace matters. Key responsibilities: Advising on the interpretation and application of agreements, policies and procedures; case management from a VPFAL perspective of workplace and student complaints, and grievances, involving faculty members and librarians; drafting letters; providing support to University bargaining committees and the process of implementation of agreements; producing a variety of reports in support of faculty relations and bargaining with UTFA; and providing related administrative support including note-taking in meetings, preparing speaking notes and keeping track of deadlines, including governance timelines. Qualifications Required: Education: University degree in a relevant discipline and course work in the Human Resources field with particular focus on labour relations/faculty relations; or equivalent combination of education and experience. An MIR/MIRHR is considered an asset. Experience: Minimum three (3) years' related human resources experience with an emphasis on collective agreement and employment policy interpretation and application, grievance/arbitration processes, and workplace complaints and investigations. Experience in Academic HR in a university context is considered an asset. Demonstrated experience advising internal clients in policy interpretation and with employee investigations and case management. Knowledge of labour and employment law, including the Ontario Human Rights Code. Experience working with diverse populations including demonstrated effective consultation skills with designated groups. Sound knowledge of human resources best practices and familiarity with public sector employment. Must have previous experience data management. Significant knowledge of HR principles and practices and, preferably, knowledge of the University’s policies and practices as they pertain to faculty members and librarians. Skills: Computer experience including word processing, spreadsheet applications, database management, and scheduling software (e.g, Outlook). Internet research skills required. Other: Excellent oral and written communication, interpersonal and organizational skills. Excellent analytical skills. Ability to exercise tact, independent judgement and discretion. Ability to handle sensitive client interactions effectively and with professionalism. Ability to maintain strict confidentiality and to handle sensitive information in an appropriate manner. Ability to understand and synthesize information and statistics. Demonstrated ability to prioritize a fluctuating workload, under pressure, and to meet deadlines. Accuracy and attention to detail essential. Ability to work both independently and within a team environment. Closing Date: 10/13/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 3 -- Hiring Zone: $93,592 - $109,190 -- Broadband Salary Range: $93,592  - $155,985 Job Category: People, Finance & Digital Services Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Database, Internet Research, Law, Administrative Assistant, Consulting, Technology, Research, Legal, Administrative, Contract Apply now » Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
    },
