    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Manager%2C-Finance-and-Administration-ON/606613117/": {
      "title": "Manager, Finance and Administration Job Details",
      "description": "Manager, Finance and Administration Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Manager, Finance and Administration Date Posted: 09/30/2026 Req ID: 50390 Faculty/Division: University of Toronto Scarborough Department: UTSC:Business Development Campus: University of Toronto Scarborough (UTSC) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: ABOUT US The University of Toronto Scarborough is a place of energy, enthusiasm and passion. Our commitment to inclusive excellence attracts the brightest learners, scholars and employees from around the globe. Our success has been made possible by the opportunity given to us by Indigenous hosts to operate on their territory, and we cherish our continuing partnerships with these communities. The University of Toronto Scarborough is an exciting campus with unlimited potential. Join us on our journey. The Department of Business Development provides the following services: Academic Printing and Custom Publishing Services Retail & Conference Services Food and Beverage Services TCard Services Internal Events Services Miller Lash House Services The department also manages the relationship with the U of T Bookstore and the N'sheemaehn Child Care Centre on campus. Our department is broad in scope and our collective goal is to provide quality services that satisfy the multi-faceted needs of our, students, faculty, staff and external clients. We continually evaluate the effectiveness of our existing services, makes changes as required, and look for new business opportunities and services that can contribute to life at UTSC. This search aligns with the University’s commitment to strategically and proactively promote diversity among our community members ( Statement on Equity, Diversity & Excellence ). Recognizing that Black, Indigenous, and other Racialized communities have experienced inequities that have developed historically and are ongoing, we strongly welcome and encourage candidates from those communities to apply. YOUR OPPORTUNITY Under the general direction of the Director, the Manager, Finance and Administration is responsible for the management of complex financial and administration functions required to meet the goals and objectives of the Business Development Department. In this role, the Manager, Finance and Administration assists and advises the Director on financial strategies for the department, develops, manages and monitors operating, ancillary, and self-funded budgets and provides operational management and human resources management within the department. The Manager, Finance is an active participant in the department’s strategic planning process. YOUR RESPONSIBILITIES Key responsibilities include: preparing budgets for units in the department; forecasting revenues and expenditures; conducting financial analyses and making recommendations to address budget implications; developing and implementing business process improvements; reviewing financial controls to ensure financial integrity; budget modeling; and assuming overall responsibility for human resources related to the department’s administrative staff. The Manager, Finance and Administration manages the department’s financial administration staff, including hiring, supervision and performance management. The Manager, Finance and Administration provides oversight to the department’s financial, administrative and central service functions. The Manager, Finance and Administration oversees the Department’s budgets (operating, ancillary and self-funded), financial processes and financial forecasting. The Manager, Finance and Administration works collaboratively with the department’s management team. The Manager, Finance and Administration leads operational projects, financial performance reviews and the purchasing and administration of the department’s computer equipment and other assets. ESSENTIAL QUALIFICATIONS EDUCATION: University degree and a professional accounting certification and/or an equivalent combination of education and experience. EXPERIENCE: Must have a minimum of five years of relevant and progressive experience in financial management and administration, preferably in a post-secondary environment. Must have demonstrated experience managing complex budgets. Must have experience administering accounting policies and procurement policies; providing financial advice to senior management, and participating in strategic planning. Must have experience managing staff in a unionized environment. ASSET: Working knowledge of University of Toronto policies and procedures and their application. SKILLS: Must be proficient in MS Office software (Excel and Word) and advanced knowledge of finance and accounting. Sound working knowledge of FIS and HRIS (SAP) or equivalent systems is essential. Must have excellent: organizational and time management skills, oral and written communication skills, analytical, problem-solving, and financial and administrative skills. Must also have excellent oral and written communication skills. OTHER: Must be able to manage competing deadlines and a variety of complex projects simultaneously. Must be willing to respond to/and manage shifting priorities. Must be service oriented and responsive to the needs of the department and their clients. Must have the ability to adapt to new technology and to work effectively in an interdisciplinary environment and keep up-to-date on the rapid changes in the University environment. Applicants are expected to show evidence of a commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, and the promotion of a respectful and collegial learning and working environment. Closing Date: 10/09/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 3 -- Hiring Zone: $97,336 - $113,558 -- Broadband Salary Range: $97,336 - $162,224 Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: HR, HRIS, Performance Management, Manager, Financial, Human Resources, Management, Finance Apply now » Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
    },
    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Scarborough-Project-Coordinator-and-Designer-ON/606612917/": {
      "title": "Project Coordinator and Designer",
      "description": "Project Coordinator and Designer Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Project Coordinator and Designer Date Posted: 09/30/2026 Req ID: 50384 Faculty/Division: UofT Scarborough Department: UTSC:Facilities Management Campus: University of Toronto Scarborough (UTSC) Position Number: 00059313 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The University of Toronto Scarborough is a place of energy, enthusiasm and passion. Our commitment to inclusive excellence attracts the brightest learners, scholars and employees from around the globe. Our success has been made possible by the opportunity given to us by Indigenous hosts to operate on their territory, and we cherish our continuing partnerships with these communities. The University of Toronto Scarborough is an exciting campus with unlimited potential. Join us on our journey. In the Facilities Management department, we take pride in our buildings and grounds and provide a welcoming, service-oriented, clean and safe environment for our students, faculty and staff. Our mission is to facilitate the Academic Mission of Excellence in Research and Teaching by providing a safe, clean, healthy, comfortable and sustainable environment for students, faculty, staff and visitors. This search aligns with the University’s commitment to strategically and proactively promote diversity among our community members ( Statement on Equity, Diversity & Excellence ). Recognizing that Black, Indigenous, and other Racialized communities have experienced inequities that have developed historically and are ongoing, we strongly welcome and encourage candidates from those communities to apply. Your opportunity: The Project Coordinator and Designer provides project coordination and design support for capital and renewal projects undertaken by the Facilities Management Department. Working under the direction of the Manager of Facilities Assets & Utilities Planning, the role supports projects from planning and design through tendering, construction and close-out. The incumbent supports project management activities, including coordinating consultants and stakeholders, managing assigned project tasks, and assisting with construction administration such as site reviews and documentation. Responsibilities also include design investigations, preparation of tender and permit document sets, and development and coordination of electrical system designs. The role works collaboratively with internal clients and stakeholders to develop responses to varied and complex program requirements. This includes space program analysis, test fits, layouts, data sets, 3D models, and supporting documentation. The Project Coordinator and Designer also assist in maintaining coordinated project documentation and materials across multiple capital projects. Your responsibilities will include: Liaising between stakeholders and/or contractors Producing technical documentation and CAD drawings for approval Developing technical specifications for inclusion on CAD drawings Liaising with clients to ensure designs reflect operational requirements Checking the accuracy and compatibility of design elements Developing viable design solutions and artistic renderings Essential Qualifications: Advanced college diploma in technology, engineering or related field, or an acceptable equivalent combination of education and experience. Minimum four years of related experience in Institutional design with an emphasis on complex interior projects. Sound knowledge and demonstrated experience of architectural, technical and graphic representation and graphic layout is required. Demonstrated ability to create 3D modelling at an intermediate level in Sketchup, AutoCad, or other similar software. Demonstrated ability to design and layout graphic materials for presentation and/or publication. Demonstrated experience in planning and design of systems furniture. Experience in the review of specifications, shop drawings and site (field) review of projects during construction. Demonstrated success in building collaborative relationships with internal and external stakeholders. Excellent computer skills including AutoCAD with experience in the preparation of architectural drawings, Google Sketchup, Microsoft Office, Excel and Adobe Creative Suite (InDesign, Illustrator, Photoshop). Strong interpersonal and verbal and written communication skills. Exceptional attention to detail with the ability to generate new ideas. Must have a passion for quality and design excellence, artistic ability. Strong organizational and analytical skills Evidence of leadership, initiative, diplomacy and excellent judgement. Ability to set priorities and targets and to meet deadlines in relation to frequently changing demands. Applicants are also expected to show evidence of a commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, and the promotion of a respectful and collegial learning and working environment. Assets (Nonessential): Experience with Laboratory and Classroom design is desirable. Professional Degree in Engineering with ability to track towards P.Eng. licensure strongly preferred. To be successful in this role you will be: Accountable Communicator Multi-tasker Problem solver Team player Notes : This is an 18-month term position. The hours of work for this position are: Monday - Friday, 8:00 am to 4:15 pm. This role is currently eligible for a hybrid work arrangement, pursuant to University policies and guidelines, including but not limited to the University of Toronto's Alternative Work Arrangements Guideline . Closing Date: 10/08/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 12 -- $84,564 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $108,145. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Engineering / Technical Divisional HR Office Email: humanresources.utsc@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: AutoCAD, CAD, Drafting, Electrical, Graphic Design, Engineering, Creative Apply now » Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
