    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Mississauga-Department-Manager-ON/606632117/": {
      "title": "Department Manager Job Details",
      "description": "Department Manager Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Department Manager Date Posted: 09/30/2026 Req ID: 50399 Faculty/Division: UofT Mississauga Department: UTM: Visual Studies Campus: University of Toronto Mississauga (UTM) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: U of T Mississauga—the second largest campus of Canada’s top-ranked university and the only research university in Ontario’s booming Peel Region—is one of the world’s great catalysts of human potential. Our employee community hums with the energy of 3,400 faculty, librarians and staff, who power our campus with curiosity, connection and care. We work together to spark life-changing research and innovation, make an indelible mark on the world by building equitable cities and societies, enable healthy lives, create a sustainable future and ignite entrepreneurship. Above all, we prioritize student success, and seek to give our 16,500 students the lift of a lifetime through learning and discovery. We love to open opportunities available nowhere else for our community to achieve their ambitions and make their unique contributions to Canada and the world. This work all comes together on a spectacularly green campus, alongside the Missinihe-ziibi (Trusting Creek or Credit River), where we seek to honour truth, reciprocity and reconciliation on the traditional land of the Huron-Wendat, Seneca and the Mississaugas of the Credit First Nation. We’re thrilled to welcome those who want to learn more about us and to be part of what we do. POSITION SUMMARY Reporting to the Chair, the Department Manager will assume responsibility for the administrative, financial and operational management of the Department of Visual Studies, which includes the Blackwood Gallery. The Department Manager is accountable to the Office of the CAO and serves as a primary designate with respect to human resources, finance, information technology, facilities and space planning and management. Duties will involve effective: budget and financial management providing proactive advice to the Chair by identifying and planning initiatives to meet current and emerging financial administration; administrative management of academic departmental functions; human resources management including administration of collective agreements, employment policies and protocols; allocation of space; tactical involvement with facilities and procurement, and management of information technology needs. The incumbent will participate as a representative of the department in broader strategic management initiatives related to business continuity planning and working with the Chair to develop strategic plans for departmental academic programs. The Department Manager is required to have a strong understanding of the internal workings and policies of the University to effectively manage the day-to-day operations and provide support to senior faculty administrators ensuring administrative practices are in compliance with Collective Agreements, University and Legislated policies and regulations. The role assumes administrative responsibility in support of the academic and research missions of the Department of Visual Studies. The Department Manager will assist in the development and implementation of proposals for new administrative and academic initiatives, timelines and budgets for projects and, as required, provide managerial support to these projects; facilitates interaction and communication amongst staff and ensures that appropriate resources are provided to administrative support staff. It is necessary for the Department Manager to interact with faculty, staff and students in a way that builds a positive departmental culture and to work collaboratively with other departments and offices within UTM and the University. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS EDUCATION University Degree in commerce/business or related discipline with a specialization in accounting; prefer professional accounting designation (CA, CMA, CGA) or in the final stages of certification, and/or acceptable equivalent combination of education and experience. EXPERIENCE Minimum five years’ related experience in a senior level position with a strong accounting/financial management responsibility. Experience in moderately complex budgeting, forecasting, auditing and analysis, and interpreting and applying policies and procedures, processing financial transactions, generating financial reports from a financial system, reconciling financial information, and process improvement. Demonstrated experience managing financial, physical and human resources. Experience administering policies and collective agreements; strategic planning experience regarding all aspects of Departmental structure, programs (administrative and academic) and services. Management and supervisory experience required. SKILLS Advanced knowledge of spreadsheet applications and good knowledge of word processing software, preferably in Excel and Microsoft Word required. Experience with the University’s Financial Information system (FIS), Research Information System (RIS) and Human Resource Information System (HRIS) or similar systems a strong asset. Demonstrated knowledge of advanced management and financial accounting, statistics, business finance, Canadian income taxation and internal controls. Excellent decision-making and presentation skills. OTHER Excellent interpersonal, communication (verbal and written) organizational and time management skills; strong leadership and team building skills; ability to exercise sound judgment, tact and initiative; high level of attention to detail and accuracy and demonstrated commitment to service; demonstrated ability to deal effectively with staff and faculty at all levels of the organization; ability to maintain confidentiality. Ability to analyze large amounts of complex data and make recommendations based on findings. Experience applying general accepted accounting principles and practices within a public sector environment; experience in fund research accounting an asset. Working knowledge of policies and procedures of the University of Toronto and their application with the University of Toronto Mississauga. **This position is available on a term basis ending August 2028** Closing Date: 10/09/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 3 -- Hiring Zone: $93,592 - $109,190 -- Broadband Salary Range: $93,592  - $155,985 Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Sustainability, Business Process, Information Systems, HRIS, Energy, Management, Technology, Research, Human Resources Apply now » Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
