ologist Date Posted: 10/01/2026 Closing Date: 11/05/2026 , 11:59PM ET Req ID: 50356 Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Obstetrics&Gynaecology Hospital Affiliation: Sunnybrook Health Science Centre Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology, Temerty Faculty of Medicine at the University of Toronto, and the Division of Gynecologic Oncology at Sunnybrook Health Sciences Centre are seeking a full-time Gynecologic Oncologist. The successful candidate will have an academic position description as a Clinician Investigator, Clinician Educator, or Clinician Quality Improvement and must be eligible for a full-time clinical academic appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor at the University of Toronto. The anticipated start date is July 1, 2027 , or another mutually agreeable date. The University of Toronto Division of Gynecologic Oncology provides comprehensive, multidisciplinary care to patients with gynecologic malignancies and is committed to excellence in clinical care, teaching, clinical trials, and research. The Division includes more than 20 Gynecologic Oncologists across four affiliated cancer centres, serving a metropolitan population of m ore than 6.5 million people. The successful candidate will join an established team of six Gynecologic Oncologists based at Sunnybrook Health Sciences Centre, a fully affiliated teaching hospital of the University of Toronto and home to the Odette Cancer Centre and Sunnybrook Research Institute. As a member of an accomplished interprofessional team, the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to collegial and collaborative practice, with excellent communication skills and a passion for delivering outstanding patient care in a multidisciplinary environment. We are seeking a candidate with an excellent track record of academic productivity and peer-reviewed publications who will continue to contribute to a strong and sustained research program. The successful candidate will also demonstrate advanced surgical skills, including expertise in open and minimally invasive (laparoscopic and robotic) surgery. Enthusiastic participation in all levels of our teaching and education mandate, including undergraduate, residency, and fellowship education, is expected. The successful candidate will promote and demonstrate excellence in professional practice and conduct. Candidates must be licensed, or eligible for licensure with the College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario. Qualified applicants must be certified, or eligible for certification, in the subspecialty of Gynecologic Oncology by the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada (RCPSC), or have completed equivalent regulated subspecialty training in Gynecologic Oncology, in addition to an MD degree. This position is funded through the provincial Alternate Payment Plan in Gynecologic Oncology. Compensation for this position will be commensurate with qualifications and experience and will be composed of fee for service, an alternative funding plan and academic salary as per GOGO provincial agreement. The salary range of this position exceeds $200,000 CAD per annum. Applications will be accepted until November 5 , 2026, or until the position is filled. Suitably qualified candidates are invited to apply with a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, and the name of three referees/ three support letters via email to: Dr. Danielle Vicus Odette Cancer Centre Division Head, Gynecologic Oncology Professor of OBGYN, University of Toronto 2075 Bayview Avenue Toronto, ON M4N 3M5 Email: danielle.vicus@sunnybrook.ca CAUTION: This ad is “posted only” to the U of T affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Oncology, Obstetrics, Patient Care, Academic, Healthcare, Research, Education Apply now » Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
    },
    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Mississauga-Collections-Officer-ON/606653317/": {
      "title": "Collections Officer Job Details",
      "description": "Collections Officer Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Collections Officer Date Posted: 10/01/2026 Req ID: 50400 Faculty/Division: UofT Mississauga Department: UTM: Anthropology Campus: University of Toronto Mississauga (UTM) Position Number: 00059922 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: U of T Mississauga—the second largest campus of Canada’s top-ranked university and the only research university in Ontario’s booming Peel Region—is one of the world’s great catalysts of human potential. Our employee community hums with the energy of 3,400 faculty, librarians and staff, who power our campus with curiosity, connection and care. We work together to spark life-changing research and innovation, make an indelible mark on the world by building equitable cities and societies, enable healthy lives, create a sustainable future and ignite entrepreneurship. Above all, we prioritize student success, and seek to give our 16,500 students the lift of a lifetime through learning and discovery. We love to open opportunities available nowhere else for our community to achieve their ambitions and make their unique contributions to Canada and the world. This work all comes together on a spectacularly green campus, alongside the Missinihe-ziibi (Trusting Creek or Credit River), where we seek to honour truth, reciprocity and reconciliation on the traditional land of the Huron-Wendat, Seneca and the Mississaugas of the Credit First Nation. We’re thrilled to welcome those who want to learn more about us and to be part of what we do. Working Hours: Monday-Friday 8:45am- 5:00pm. This role is four (4) days on-site. Your opportunity: The Department of Anthropology and Office of Indigenous Initiatives (OII) at UTM is seeking an Indigenous-Centred Collections Officer to play a pivotal role in transforming the stewardship of archaeological and cultural collections through Indigenous direction, collaboration, and relationship-building. The role of the Collections Officer reports to both the Department Manager in the Department of Anthropology and the Director of Indigenous Initiatives in the OII. The successful candidate will help guide consultation, repatriation, rematriation, or long-term stewardship processes for archaeological belongings originating from Indigenous territories across what is now known as Ontario. This position offers a unique opportunity to build meaningful partnerships with Indigenous Nations, support reconciliation commitments, and helps shape community-directed approaches to belongings and collections stewardship and coordination that honours Indigenous rights, knowledge, and governance. Your responsibilities will include: Oversee the organization, documentation, and curation of Indigenous ancestral archaeological belongings Coordinate Indigenous-directed consultation and relationship-building with Indigenous Nations through UTM OII Support the Department’s Collections & Data Committee in developing Indigenous-directed standard operating procedures Liaise with Indigenous communities, Anthropology department at U of T St. George campus, government partners, and other institutions Coordinate repatriation, rematriation, and collaborative stewardship processes Plan for the long-term stewardship of existing and future collections Manage logistical aspects of stewardship and repatriation processes, including packaging, shipping coordination, and preparation of materials for transfer in collaboration with relevant institutional units Occasional travel within Canada may be required to support consultation and repatriation or rematriation processes Essential Qualifications: Master's Degree or acceptable combination of equivalent education and experience. Six to seven years of progressive experience in collections management, archaeological or cultural heritage stewardship Demonstrated experience in indigenous engagement and/or consultation Demonstrated experience navigating repatriation/rematriation processes, preferrably working directly with or within indigenous communities Indigenous membership or citizenship, and/or lived experience with Indigenous communities, demonstrated commitment as an Indigenous ally, and strong cultural competency. Familiarity with Indigenous protocols and practices of community engagement and respect for Indigenous governance structures and data sovereignty in Canada Understanding of Canadian legislative frameworks related to archaeological stewardship and repatriation Training or experience in museum studies, collections management, or archaeological practice, including those licensed to practice archaeology in Ontario To be successful in this role you will be: Adaptable Communicator Cooperative Diplomatic Problem solver Responsible Tactful Closing Date: 10/29/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 14 -- $95,344 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $121,932. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Scientific, Anthropology, Collections, Accounts Receivable, Sustainability, Engineering, Social Sciences, Finance, Energy Apply now » Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
    },
