rofessor - Academic Psychiatrist - Addictions Date Posted: 09/30/2026 Closing Date: 11/20/2026 , 11:59PM ET, Open Until Filled Req ID: 50392 Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Psychiatry Hospital Affiliation: Centre for Addiction & Mental Health Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Description: Lecturer/Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Academic Psychiatrist - Addictions Division:  Gambling and Technology use and Addiction Psychiatry in child and youth and adult populations The Department of Psychiatry, Faculty of Medicine at the University of Toronto and the Department of Psychiatry of The Centre for Addiction and Mental Health (CAMH), are seeking to recruit an Academic Psychiatrist Physician – Addictions Division.  The successful candidate will have an academic position description of Clinician Investigator and must be eligible for a full-time clinical academic appointment at the rank of Assistant, Associate or Full Professor at the University of Toronto, with an anticipated start date of January 1, 2027 or shortly thereafter. The Centre for Addiction and Mental Health (CAMH) is Canada’s largest mental health teaching hospital and one of the world’s leading research centres in its field. CAMH is fully affiliated with the University of Toronto and is a Pan America Health Organization/World Health Organization Collaborating Centre. With a dedicated staff of more than 4,000 physicians, clinicians, researchers, educators and support staff, CAMH offers outstanding clinical care to more than 37,000 patients each year and over 118 inpatient and outpatient clinical programs. The organization conducts ground-breaking research through its 11 research centres and provides expert training to over 13,000 health care professionals and scientists. In addition, CAMH delivers education programs to over 40,000 healthcare professionals each year and advocates on public policy issues at all levels of government. The successful applicant must hold an MD degree, must be Board certified or Board Eligible in Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada Specialty, and must be eligible for medical licensure or academic licensure with the College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario.  The successful candidate will have expertise in gambling and technology use in child and youth and adult populations. The successful candidate will have Addiction Medicine training and expertise in vaping and tobacco is preferred as well as a record of excellence in scholarship.  The successful candidate will have a scholarly interest in collaborative and integrated care delivery, measurement-based care and the use of digital technology in facilitating healthcare access and experience working collaboratively with clinicians on program design, research projects and research implementation. The successful candidate will ideally have experience and strong interest in collaborative care for the treatment of concurrent disorders. The salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. The salary range of this position exceeds $200,000 CAD per annum. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply by October 18, 2026.  Applications will be accepted until the position is filled.   Should you be interested in this opportunity, please forward a one-page statement of interest, curriculum vitae and the names and contact information of three referees via email to: Dr. Leslie Buckley Chief, Addictions Division The Centre for Addiction and Mental Health 1001 Queen Street West, Toronto, ON Tel: 416-535-8501 e-mail: leslie.buckley@camh.ca For more information on the University of Toronto, Department of Psychiatry, please visit http://www.psychiatry.utoronto.ca . For more information about Centre for Addiction and Mental Health (CAMH), please visit https://www.camh.ca/ . CAUTION: This ad is “posted only” to the U of T affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Psychology, Counseling, Public Policy, Academic, Healthcare, Legal, Government, Education Apply now » Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
