      "description": "Administrative & Financial Assistant Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Administrative & Financial Assistant Date Posted: 09/30/2026 Req ID: 50348 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Arts & Science Department: Technoscience Research Unit Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00059844 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Technoscience Research Unit (TRU) at the University of Toronto is an Indigenous-led home for critical and creative research on science, technology and environment. Led by M. Murphy and Kristen Bos, the TRUhas an internationally recognized focus on Indigenous Science and Technology Studies, Environmental Justice, Indigenous Environmental Data Justice, and community-based research. The TRU is home to multiple labs and projects, including the Environmental Data Justice Lab, with a focus on Indigenous community-based research in Canada’s Chemical Valley and the Indigenous Science and Ethical Substance Lab, which undertakes research in the areas of policy, methods, and practices concerning pollutants andenvironmental justice, and data justice. The TRU is dedicated to co-building decolonial, justice-oriented, and feminist research community and supports a diverse community of researchers, students and community researchers. The TRU is affiliated with theSchool of Environment and has a partnership with the Acceleration Consortium, and is home to the NFRF funded project All Our Chemical Relations. Your opportunity: Under the general direction of the Department Manager and TRU Directors, you will provide comprehensive administrative support to an Indigenous-led research unit guided by values-based research practices in a highly collaborative and fast-paced environment. Responsibilities include serving as the first point of contact by responding to inquiries from a diverse range of stakeholders; coordinating financial processes such as expense reimbursements, debit memos, purchase requisitions and orders, invoice payments, bank deposits, timesheet administration, monitoring account and monthly statement reconciliations and ensuring compliance with the University's Guide to Financial Management. The role also supports meeting coordination, space management, onboarding activities, and records management in accordance with Indigenous data governance principles. Your responsibilities will include: Supports front line activities and acts as first point of contact for inquiries Proofreading and fact-checking content; Handling sensitive and/or confidential information Determining actionable items based on the review of applicable information Supports reimbursements, purchasing, financial analysis and/or reporting activities Determining logistical details and activities for events; arranging catering and accommodations Maintaining TRU Directors calendars, and scheduling appointments/activities, and resolving scheduling conflicts Essential Qualifications: Advanced College Diploma (3 years) or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum five (5) years of relevant experience in a combination of administrative, event planning, and financial administration. Demonstrated experience working in an Indigenous and/or marginalized community-based research environments. Experience with OCAP and Indigenous data governance. Experience generating financial reports, monitoring and reconciling research grant accounts, and knowledge of the University Guide to Financial Management. Experience managing complex schedule/calendar for multiple stakeholders, with strong organization skills. ⁠Experience taking meeting minutes and disseminating information. Experience arranging domestic and international business trips, including making travel and hotel arrangements and preparing expense reimbursements. Experience with event planning and logistics support. Experience with maintaining information on digital platforms and websites. Excellent verbal and written communication, interpersonal, and service delivery, with experience supporting diverse needs in interactions with students, faculty, staff, and external stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to exercise a high degree of initiative, political acuity, sound judgment and sensitivity dealing with a variety of responsibilities in a high-volume environment with multiple deadlines and competing priorities. Strong ability to work under pressure and handle a variety of tasks such as coordinating multiple processes and dealing with a large number of accounts with accuracy and attention to detail Accomplished ability to multitask and demonstrated ability to meet multiple deadlines without compromising quality. Advanced computer skills in MS Office (e.g., Word, Outlook Calendar, Excel, and PowerPoint), Adobe Acrobat and interne To be successful in this role youwill be: Accountable Diligent Multi-tasker Organized Problem solver Team player Closing Date: 10/08/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Grant - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 10 -- $75,004 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $95,915. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Chemical Research, Event Planning, Proofreading, Copy Editor, Administrative Assistant, Engineering, Hospitality, Creative, Administrative Apply now » Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
