      "description": "Director, Academic Human Resources Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Director, Academic Human Resources Date Posted: 10/02/2026 Req ID: 50406 Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Human Resources, Academic Campus : St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About Us The Temerty Faculty of Medicine at the University of Toronto is at the centre of one of North America’s largest biomedical research, education and clinical care networks. With 14 fully affiliated research-intensive hospitals — and dozens more community and clinical care sites — Temerty Medicine offers unparalleled opportunities in Canada’s most dynamic city for our more than 9,000 faculty and staff and 7,000 learners at all levels. Your Opportunity As Director, Academic Human Resources, you will provide strategic leadership, management, and vision for academic Human Resources services across the Temerty Faculty of Medicine. Serving as a vital bridge between the Faculty and university-wide leadership, you will inspire and mentor a high-performing administrative team who deliver frontline counsel and guidance on academic policies across more than 40 academic and administrative units. Reporting to the Chief Administrative Officer and acting as a key strategic partner to the Office of the Dean, your team will expertly guide faculty leadership through the complex appointment, review, and promotion lifecycle for our extensive network of over 9,000 faculty members. Along with advising on appointment offers for senior academic administrators and designing and implementing impactful onboarding experiences for chairs and directors, you will champion the Faculty's Academic Strategic Plan. Leveraging your operational insights, you will provide strategic support for new initiatives, task forces, and committees, playing an instrumental role in driving timely outcomes for key deliverables. Through this work, you will advance our commitment to equity, diversity, and inclusion, helping to shape the Faculty's long-term strategic vision. Essential Qualifications Graduate degree or equivalent combination of education and experience Minimum ten years senior administrative experience within a university setting, including a deep familiarity with the academic HR life cycle, tenure process, and University academic HR norms Demonstrated experience in liaising with senior leaders, responding to and handling matters of a complex, confidential and sensitive nature Demonstrated professional experience in understanding complex issues related to organizational policies and practices Proven experience leading change and driving results through process evaluation and redesign Proven experience developing, leading, and mentoring high-functioning teams Experience interpreting human resources policies, legislation, and guidelines Demonstrated success in implementing equity and diversity initiatives across a complex multi-sector environment Data-driven with experience using various tools, performance metrics and approaches for analysis, decision-making and reporting Strong technical skills, including knowledge of the University of Toronto’s Administrative Management System (AMS) and a facility for working with project management tools and keeping current with new and emerging technologies Strong leadership skills with ability to engage, secure support, commitment and results from others Outstanding interpersonal, communication and presentation skills Demonstrated knowledge of HR best practices and demonstrated commitment to the promotion of equity and inclusiveness in the workplace and the ability to work effectively with all constituents in a highly diverse community Ability to influence and present ‘win/win’ solutions to effect change and problem-solve in a highly collegial setting Strong integrative skills related to understanding cross functional implications and interrelationships of issues and decisions Proven ability to work with a high degree of independence solving complex problems Must be able to move complex initiatives forward in situations characterized by high levels of ambiguity and political sensitivity Must exhibit a high degree of diplomacy and tact in all situations Assets (Nonessential) Deep knowledge of the academic HR life cycle for clinical (MD) and non-clinical faculty, strongly preferred Understanding of University governance, educational priorities, policy formation, legal obligations, reporting requirements and planning protocol Closing Date: 10/23/2026,11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 7 -- Hiring Zone: $145,219 - $169,423 -- Broadband Salary Range: $145,219 - $242,032 Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: HR Manager, Human Resources Director, HR, Project Manager, Manager, Human Resources, Technology, Management Apply now » Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
