    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Lab-Coordinator-%28term%29-ON/606698017/": {
      "title": "Lab Coordinator (term)",
      "description": "Lab Coordinator (term) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Lab Coordinator (term) Date Posted: 10/02/2026 Req ID: 50416 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Arts & Science Department: Dept of Psychology Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00051750 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Faculty of Arts & Science is the heart of Canada’s leading university and one of the most comprehensive and diverse academic divisions in the world. The strength of Arts & Science derives from our combined teaching and research excellence in the humanities, sciences and social sciences across 29 departments, seven colleges and 46 interdisciplinary centres, institutes and programs. We can only realize our mission with the dedication and excellence of engaged staff and faculty. The diversity of opportunities and perspectives within the Faculty reflect the local and global landscape and the need for curiosity, innovative thinking and collaboration. At Arts & Science, we take pride in our legacy of innovation and discovery that has changed the way we think about the world. Established in 1927, the Department of Psychology has for more than a century been a top choice for those pursuing a career in psychological research. The combined expertise of our faculty spans all major areas of psychology and reflects a wide range of approaches to the study of mind, brain and behaviour. Our department comprises a diverse and internationally recognized faculty, first-rate laboratory facilities anda tradition of cutting-edge, collaborative research in an inspiring intellectual atmosphere. The Einstein Lab (Dr. Gillian Einstein) studies how the structure and function of the brain is influenced by the context of people’s lives, especially sex and gender. These influences include hormones and genes, as well as culture, social environment and personal life experiences. In turn, these factors can influence our health and successful aging (https://einsteinlab.ca/). Your opportunity: Under the supervision of the Principal Investigator (PI), the Lab Coordinator is responsible for the smooth day-to-day operation of the lab, involving the acquisition of data on cognition and brain response. The incumbent ensures participants and/or testing rooms are not double-booked, forms are available to sign and payments/participation credits are processed. Duties include but are not limited to recruiting participants; preparing test materials; scheduling andkeeping track of participants’ appointments and their compensation; interacting with research assistants about their duties. The Lab Coordinator is also responsible for general maintenance of the research lab; ensuring supplies are adequately stocked; compiling receipts and forms; ensuring reference libraries are maintained; lab manuals updated and maintained; files/website updated; back up information weekly; contacting departmental computer staff to ensure programs and computers run properly. Additionally, the incumbent performs other administrative duties such as maintaining a tidy environment and providing administrative support to PI, assisting with ethics protocols and grants, and assisting graduate students with participant testingand data collating. Note: this is a two-year term opportunity. Your responsibilities will include: Proofing and posting adverts to recruit applicants Preparing consent forms using templates Disseminating and collecting researchsurveys and questionnaires Generating reports Coordinating meeting schedules, agendas, materials, action and follow-up items Responding to enquiries within the defined scope of the role and redirecting as appropriate Recording or verifying transactions on a single account Providing orientation to others on work procedures and practices Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum two (2) years of relevant experience in a research lab or as a lab coordinator with knowledge of research methodology. Experience working with participants and collecting data/samples. Experience in trouble-shooting various technologies along with website maintenance. Experience interacting with participants and students of diverse backgrounds. Strong computer skills including with Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint. Strong interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. Sound time-management, organizational skills, and ability to multi-task. Demonstrated ability to work under pressure to meet multiple competing deadlines. Strong attention to detail, ability to use sound judgment, and proven ability to work within a team. Assets (Nonessential): Demonstrated knowledge in SPSS, Matlab, EPrime, BrainVoyager, and WordPress preferred. To be successful in this role you will be: Communicator Efficient Goal oriented Multi-tasker Organized Problem solver For internal staff, a copy of the detailed job description is available upon request from the Faculty of Arts and Science HR Office by emailing: adminhr.artsci@utoronto.ca . Closing Date: 10/19/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Grant - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 07 -- $62,646 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $80,116. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Research Administration & Teaching Divisional HR Office Email: adminhr.artsci@utoronto.ca Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Laboratory, Administrative Assistant, Equity, Science, Administrative, Research, Finance Apply now » Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
    },
    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Data-Analyst%2C-Teaching-&-Learning-ON/606706417/": {
      "title": "Data Analyst, Teaching & Learning",
      "description": "Data Analyst, Teaching & Learning Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Data Analyst, Teaching & Learning Date Posted: 10/02/2026 Req ID: 50419 Faculty/Division: VP & Provost Department: Vice-Provost, Teaching & Learning Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00051167 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Office of the Vice-Provost, Teaching & Learning (OVPTL) (formerly known as Office of the Vice-Provost: Innovation in Undergraduate Education) supports ongoing and new efforts to enhance the quality and expand the reach of high-impact teaching and learning practices at the University of Toronto. To support teaching and learning across the University, the OVPTL maintains a robust profile related to five key priorities: 1. Teaching Awards & Grants: Recognizing and funding staff and faculty who demonstrate commitment to innovation and excellence in teaching practices. 2. Curriculum Development: Working with institutional and divisional stakeholders to develop and assess course and program-level outcomes. 3. Teaching Initiatives: Stewarding the development of institutional frameworks and resources for innovative teaching practices, such as experiential learning, undergraduate research and generative artificial intelligence in teaching and learning. 4. Digital Transformation: Building and supporting systems that enable faculty, staff and students to achieve their academic goals. 5. Analytics: Leveraging data to enhance program planning, decision-making and student success. Your opportunity: Reporting to the Manager, Student Success Analytics, the Data Analyst, Teaching & Learning, will be part of a dynamic, collaborative, and innovative group focused on enhancing undergraduate student academic success at the University. By utilizing existing data tools and creating customized analyses and visualizations, you will identify areas of opportunity to support student retention, progression, and graduation for undergraduate students at the University of Toronto. Current priorities include establishing and supporting a sustainable institutional reporting and analytics framework, enabling the University to use student engagement data for institutional planning, student success initiatives, and unit-level decision-making. This work will create institutional reporting capabilities that deliver consistent, aggregated reporting on student engagement by division; strengthen existing student success analytics by integrating engagement indicators with retention, progression, and graduation data; and develop a standard assessment and planning package using a common baseline set of reports. The role will also contribute to other institutional projects that support the teaching and learning environment, potentially including the University’s Learning Analytics efforts using data from the learning management system (Canvas, known as Quercus at U of T), and other projects that provide key data insights to instructors, staff and academic leaders to support data-informed decisions that enhance teaching and learning. Across projects, the Analyst will consult with specialists on the data-driven design of student learning initiatives producing reports and analyses, and will have the opportunity to build new data tools that improve the student learning experience. The ideal candidate is comfortable working with stakeholders to understand their needs, brings creative approaches to interpreting learning data through analysis and visualization. This includes experience querying databases (SQL) coding using a programming language (e.g., R or Python) and a data visualization tool (e.g., Tableau or Power BI). Your responsibilities will include: Creating and producing visual images on scientific data and research Analyzing and developing program scripts to extract, reformat and analyze data Developing and maintaining a dashboard for quick access to key performance indicators Communicating and presenting results to technical and non-technical audiences Analyzing complex data that requires great precision and attention to many details Generating reports Coordinating tasks for projects and other strategic initiatives with stakeholders Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum five years of relevant experience supporting data-driven decision-making by conducting detailed data analysis, producing complex statistical information, and analyzing large datasets, preferably in a postsecondary education or research-intensive institution 2+ Years experience developing visualizations using Tableau or Power BI Experience developing and maintaining a dashboard of key performance indicators. Experience and intermediate skills in writing/coding programming scripts (e.g. Python, SQL) to extract, reformat, and analyze data. Experience effectively synthesizing information Experience training on research methods and data analysis Experience working with and manipulating complex data sets using Excel, Tableau and R Experience with data analysis. Familiarity with Microsoft Office products, and advanced skills in Microsoft Excel. Strong oral and written communication and presentation skills. Excellent organizational and time-management skills, with the ability to adapt to new and changing priorities Project management skills with demonstrated ability to meet deadlines and to manage a set of competing priorities. Demonstrated strong client service orientation and commitment to fostering equity, diversity and inclusion in a professional environment. To be successful in this role you will be: Meticulous Multi-tasker Organized Persuasive Problem solver Self-directed Closing Date: 10/19/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 13 -- $89,794 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $114,832. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Information Technology (IT) Divisional HR Office Email: Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Data Analyst, Database, SQL, Curriculum Development, Training, Data, Technology, Education Apply now » Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
