    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Dentist-in-Chief-Department-of-Paediatric-Dentistry%2C-Hospital-for-Sick-Children-ON/606707217/": {
      "title": "Dentist-in-Chief",
      "description": "Dentist-in-Chief - Department of Paediatric Dentistry, Hospital for Sick Children Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Dentist-in-Chief - Department of Paediatric Dentistry, Hospital for Sick Children Date Posted: 10/02/2026 Closing Date: 10/30/2026 , 11:59PM ET Req ID: 50422 Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Faculty/Division: Faculty of Dentistry Department: Faculty of Dentistry Hospital Affiliation: Hospital for Sick Children Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: The Department of Paediatric Dentistry at The Hospital for Sick Children (SickKids), Faculty of Dentistry, University of Toronto, is inviting applications for the position of Dentist-in-Chief. This is a full-time role for an academic paediatric dentist and leader in paediatric oral health. The effective date of this appointment is June 2027 but can be negotiated. Primary Description Responsibilities include full clinical practice, research, and education, and administrative responsibilities as required by a Department Chief. Evidence of excellence in teaching and research is required. This role reports directly to the Chief of Peri-Operative Services. Additional Description The successful candidate should be a senior academic with an international reputation who can provide effective and collaborative leadership and vision at the hospital, provincial, national and international levels. The candidate must be eligible for appointment at the rank of Associate Professor at the University of Toronto and be eligible for certification with the Royal College of Dental Surgeons of Ontario. Candidates must obtain an appropriate Visa, if applicable. We are seeking an individual whose leadership qualifications include management proficiency, dispute resolution, communications expertise, mentoring capabilities, the ability to engender trust, function collaboratively with all manner of clinical teams and administration. Additionally, the successful candidate will have a long-term vision for the Department which integrates with the mission of Peri-Operative Services, the Hospital and the University of Toronto. Salary will be in the range of $200,000 to $400,000 for 40 hours per week, commensurate with qualifications and experience, and which will be supplemented by clinical billing activity. Benefits include Medical, Dental, Life, Group Insurance, Pension, Vision. A per annum stipend, in recognition of the administrative leadership responsibilities associated with the Department Chief role, will be provided. Support for relocation expenses will be offered. The position has a potential duration of two terms of five years each. Department Description The Department of Paediatric Dentistry at The Hospital for Sick Children consist of 18 dental surgeons, orthodontists and paediatric dentists, provides dental care for children and adolescents under 18 years whose treatment is best managed in a multidisciplinary hospital environment . It is integral to the Ontario Cleft Lip and Palate Craniofacial Dental program and is a major clinical training and research centre for the University of Toronto Graduate Paediatric Dentistry program. The Department also provides training to hospital staff, community dentists, physicians and families through affiliation with the University of Toronto. Hospital Description SickKids, located at 555 University Avenue in downtown Toronto, is among the largest children’s hospitals in North America and has a long history of excellence in clinical care, research and education. It was named the number one paediatric hospital in the world in 2025, by Newsweek magazine. SickKids is fully affiliated with the University of Toronto and is located adjacent to the University campus and to numerous specialty hospitals and biomedical research institutes. Toronto is a vibrant and multicultural city, widely recognized as one of the most diverse cities in the world, with approximately half of its residents born outside Canada and representation from more than 250 ethnicities. This diversity is reflected in the city’s neighbourhoods, food scene, Michelin-starred restaurants across Toronto and the surrounding region, and strengths in key sectors such as life sciences, finance, information, and communications technology. As one of the largest cities in North America, Toronto offers a dynamic downtown, diverse neighbourhoods, strong schools, and access to leading universities. It is regularly recognized in global city, travel, and liveability rankings. World-famous lake and wilderness country and year-round outdoor recreation are easily accessible, as are two hub airports for regional and international travel. Application Process Applications will be accepted until October 30, 2026. Should you be interested in this opportunity, please forward a one-page statement of interest [which includes the names and contact information for 3 referees] and curriculum vitae, in PDF format, via email to: Dr. Abhaya V. Kulkarni Chief, Peri-Operative Services and Chair of the Search Committee EMAIL: dentistrydepartmentchief.recruitment@sickkids.ca All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. For more information about the University of Toronto, Graduate Specialty Program of Paediatric Dentistry, please visit our home page at https://www.dentistry.utoronto.ca Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Clinic, Dental, Physician, Research, Healthcare Apply now » Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
    },
    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Athletic-Facility-Assistant-%28Term%29-ON/606712417/": {
      "title": "Athletic Facility Assistant (Term)",
      "description": "Athletic Facility Assistant (Term) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Athletic Facility Assistant (Term) Date Posted: 10/02/2026 Req ID: 50428 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Kinesiology & Physl Ed. Department: Faculty of Kinesiology & Physl Ed Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Description: Duties and Responsibilities (a) Building Security and Safety Checks membership cards (including student id cards); approves or denies entry to the facility, providing explanation of regulations as required and directs to other areas when appropriate. Permits entry of participants and spectators of events as instructed. Performs walk arounds of the indoor and outdoor facilities to monitor physical activity areas, locker rooms, shower areas, washrooms, stairwells and other public areas; checks for potential safety/security/maintenance problems, for authorized use of activity areas (per schedules) and generally for user compliance with building (and other posted) regulations; checks and secures doors as required and/or unlocks doors as specified in standard operating procedures or daily instructions; reports safety/security/maintenance deficiencies to supervisor. When Manager or Assistant Facility Manager is not available, reports emergency safety/security/maintenance to either UofT police or Physical Plant; asks unauthorized users to vacate premises; refers problems and emergencies to supervisor. Performs assigned evacuation and security duties during emergency situations. Completes log report of monitoring rounds, noting deficiencies and problems. Responds appropriately to emergency first aid and safety situations in accordance with standard operating and emergency procedures and completes appropriate injury/incident report. Performs final rounds and lock-up of buildings, according to standard operating procedure; ensures that the facility is cleared of all personnel and users before lock-up. In the absence of supervisors, assumes a lead role in maintaining the general operations of the facility ensuring work flow and appropriate coverage, reporting all action taken to the supervisors (b) Customer Service Provides general information at equipment and towel counters and by telephone re: facilities, schedules, memberships, fees, services and activities. Refers inquiries to other relevant program and/or service area as required. As a first responder, proactively stays informed of services and program changes and offerings in order to respond to conflicts or unexpected program cancellations and resolves when possible. Informs the appropriate Manager or program supervisor of the conflict requiring follow up and resolution. Books squash and tennis courts according to standard operating procedures when main office is closed. Issues and receives towels, rags, keys, recreational, fitness, intramural and intercollegiate athletic equipment to/from facility users who present proper identification according to standard operating procedures. Projects a positive professional image of the facility in dress and behavior at all times while on duty. Serves as front-line reception for complaints, emergencies and requests for assistance/service from a diverse population of members and visitors. Responds quickly to crisis situations requiring independent, timely decision making skills in a fast paced environment; handling and/or redirecting inquiries as appropriate. Provides support to part time staff in all aspects of the day to day operations. (c) General Services Assists the Managers with communication by liaising with contractors, trades people, police, fire prevention officers, caretakers, ambulance personnel, students, staff and faculty. Prepares laundry for washing according to standard operating procedures, sorts soiled laundry received, loadsand unloads laundry into commercial washing and drying machines; adds soap and cleaning agents as required; folds and hangs items on completion as necessary. Maintains and operates commercial washers, extractors and dryers, cleaning or performing minor maintenance to machines as necessary. Notifies supervisor when service personnel should be called, and liaises with service personnel to relay information for proper repairs. Maintains inventory of towels, soap, laundry chemicals, recreational, intramural and varsity athletic equipment and uniforms, records the number of cleaned towels assigned to various areas and athletic teams. Notifies supervisor when supplies are low. Responsible for the safe handling of hazardous, highly concentrated laundry chemicals. Sets up equipment and other apparatus related to the co-curricular and curricular programs such as speakers, score clocks, audiovisual equipment, flip charts, tables, chairs, bleachers, etc. in accordance with regular program schedules and special events or requests from staff and faculty with regular program schedules and special events or requests from staff and faculty. Dismantles, moves and stores activity or classroom equipment and event furnishings as required (includes operating by key, electronically controlled basketball backstops and gymnasium dividing curtains.) Ensures equipment and materials are stored in an orderly fashion, moves furniture and equipment as required including the fitness equipment storage cages and barrels filled with laundry product. Performs repairs, cleaning and preventative maintenance to exercise fitness equipment, including recharging and/or replacing batteries in score and wall clocks and batteries for fitness microphones. Maintains information in the following logs in accordance with standard operating procedures for the purposes of inventory, tracking loss, damage and usage, towel log, delivering/receiving log, repair log, key sign out, equipment maintenance and sign out, contractor log, lost and found and other related logs. Cleans lockers, removes belongings which are inappropriately stored there, records and stores items removed; helps maintain locker room cleanliness performing light housekeeping tasks. Repairs lockers i.e. install plates, numbers, etc. Performs seasonal locker clean outs, cutting locks as required; removes belongings, records and stores items removed in the designated area for pick up. Responsible for the maintenance, sanitizing and cleanliness of all relevant work areas, i.e. fitness equipment,equipment counter, towel counter, storage areas and laundry area. Receives and logs incoming deliveries and contacts the individual/ office to which the delivery is and/or delivers items appropriately addressed (d) Other Liaise with and provide service to contractors, rental groups, media, campus tours, U of T police, fire departmentand property management. May perform minor maintenance work as required. Assists with staff orientations, basic job training and performance of assigned tasks. Provides guidance andassistance to apprentices, interns and others as directed. May issue and sell guest passes when main office isclosed. May assist with mailings or promotions including folding, collating print materials (posters, notices, letters, etc.),addresses/stuffs envelopes and related items for special mailings/events. Provides input into the design and implementation of operational procedures and building projects. Other related duties as required. Minimum Requirements for Selection Education: Completion of Grade 12 or acceptable equivalent combination of education and experience. Must successfully complete a current recognized Standard First Aid, AED, and CPR certificate within the probationary period. Experience: A minimum of one year of related experience in a customer service orientated position.Familiarity with athletic facilities, equipment and/or programs. Other: Basic computer skills, ability to perform the essential physical functional requirements of the position. Mustpossess excellent oral communication skills, considerable publicrelations skills, diplomacy and tact, conflictmanagement skills; ability to deal calmly with angry or upset individuals; basic reading and writing skills; ability toexercise good judgment and initiative; ability to resolve problems; ability to participate effectively within a team; understanding of diversity and equity issues. Demonstrated ability in the following areas: following written and oral instructions; dealing courteously andeffectively with students, University staff, faculty, the public and team members; and the ability to provideinformation in a clear and concise manner. Closing Date: 10/12/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Hourly Personnel Subarea: CUPE F/T L3261 Appointment Type : Budget - Term Note: This is a term position posting. The term will end on July 3, 2026. Schedule: Full-Time Monday - Friday 6:15 am - 2:45 pm Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: Job Rate: $26.56/hr Job Category: Athletics Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Facilities, Event Planning, Housekeeping, Fitness, Operations, Hospitality, Healthcare Apply now » Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
