    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/TORONTO-Assistant-Professor-Jazz-ON/606723917/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Jazz Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Assistant Professor - Jazz Date Posted: 10/05/2026 Closing Date: 11/16/2026, 11:59PM ET Req ID: 50080 Job Category: Faculty - Tenure Stream (continuing) Faculty/Division: Faculty of Music Department: Faculty of Music Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes POSITION DESCRIPTION The Faculty of Music at the University of Toronto invites applications for a full-time tenure-stream position in the area of Jazz. The appointment will be at the rank of Assistant Professor with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. REQUIREMENTS AND QUALIFICATIONS Candidates must have earned a doctoral degree in Jazz Performance and/or Jazz Composition/Arranging, or a closely related area by the time of appointment, with a demonstrated record of excellence in research (including creative professional activities/practice) and teaching in jazz. We seek candidates whose research and teaching complement and enhance our existing departmental strengths . Candidates must provide evidence of research excellence which can be demonstrated by a record of achievement that could include: performances and/or compositions/arrangements for major venues, organizations, and festivals; collaborations with established artists and ensembles; public presence through broadcasts, recordings, and media platforms; presentations at significant academic or professional conferences; publications in top-ranked and field-relevant journals; awards and accolades; arts and/or research grants; the submitted research statement; and strong endorsements from referees. Evidence of excellence in teaching will be demonstrated through teaching accomplishments and the teaching dossier (including the required materials outlined below, as well as superior performance in other teaching-related activities), and strong letters of reference. Other teaching-related activities can include performance as a teaching assistant, course instructor or ensemble leader, experience leading successful workshops/clinics or seminars, or student mentorship. RESPONSIBILITIES The successful candidate will be expected to pursue innovative and independent research (including creative professional activities/practice), and to establish an outstanding, competitive, and externally funded research program. In addition, the successful candidate will be assigned a teaching and service load. Teaching responsibilities will include undergraduate and graduate jazz courses, including one-on-one performance lessons and/or leading jazz ensembles, as appropriate to the candidate’s areas of specialization; and research supervision and mentoring of jazz students at the masters and doctoral levels. HIRING SALARY RANGE The expected salary range is $135,000–$160,000 CAD per annum, depending on experience. Negotiations beyond this salary range will be considered for exceptionally qualified candidates. ABOUT US The Faculty of Music is a division of Canada’s largest university, located in one of the world’s most diverse cities. The Faculty of Music offers undergraduate and graduate (MMus and DMA) degrees in Jazz. For further information see music.utoronto.ca and uoftjazz.ca . APPLICATION PROCESS All application materials, including recent reference letters, must be received by November 16, 2026. All qualified candidates are invited to apply online by clicking the link below. Your CV and cover letter should be uploaded into the dedicated fields. Please combine additional application materials into one or two files in PDF/MS Word format. Links to audiovisual documentation submitted as part of the application must remain valid for the duration of the search process. Applicants must submit the following materials: a cover letter; a current curriculum vitae; a statement outlining plans for current and future research (including creative professional activities/practice) a select portfolio of recent samples of their work including stable active links to audiovisual documentation and including description of the applicant’s role in collaborative outputs a teaching dossier, including: a teaching statement sample course materials teaching evaluations or evidence of superior performance in other teaching-related activities as listed above; and the name and contact information of three references. The University of Toronto’s recruiting tool will automatically solicit and collect letters of reference from each referee within 48 hours of an application being submitted. Applicants remain responsible for ensuring that references submit recent letters (on letterhead, dated and signed) by the closing date. More details on the automatic reference letter collection, including timelines, are available in the candidate FAQ . If you have any questions about this position, please contact Dean Ryan McClelland at dean.music@utoronto.ca . All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Audio Visual, Equity, CAD, Drafting, Research, Finance, Creative, Engineering Apply now » Find similar jobs: Faculty Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
    },
    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Communications-Coordinator-ON/606723717/": {
      "title": "Communications Coordinator",
      "description": "Communications Coordinator Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Communications Coordinator Date Posted: 10/05/2026 Req ID: 50436 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Nursing Department: Lawrence Bloomberg Faculty of Nursing Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00058883 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Lawrence Bloomberg Faculty of Nursing at the University of Toronto is a globally recognized leader in nursing education, research, and practice. Our mission is to advance health through a commitment to excellence in education and research. We are dedicated to creating a supportive environment that fosters innovation and collaboration among our faculty, staff, and students. Your opportunity: This role focuses on executing strategic communication initiatives that highlight the Faculty of Nursing’s academic excellence, research impact, and community engagement. It aims to strengthen the faculty’s reputation, attract prospective students, and foster meaningful connections with stakeholders through compelling storytelling and targeted outreach. Under the functional supervision of the Senior Communications and Media Relations Officer, this position plays a key role in implementing the Faculty’s strategic communication plan. The incumbent will be responsible for coordinating project tasks and strategic initiatives with internal and external stakeholders, as well as tracking and monitoring outreach activities. Responsibilities include developing and producing promotional and outreach materials; analyzing and recommending approaches for the visual design and layout of digital assets; creating and maintaining a strong presence across social media platforms; and providing guidance on emerging social media trends to enhance digital communication strategies. The role also ensures that information on all digital platforms remains accurate, current, and aligned with the Faculty’s brand and objectives. Your responsibilities will include: Supporting digital communications activities by coordinating tasks for projects and other strategic initiatives. Responding to requests for visual material, and ensuring consistency and adherence to Faculty and University of Toronto's brand guidelines. Producing content, promotional and outreach materials for a variety of communications and marketing initiatives through print and/or online communications channels. Writing and editing digital communications for print and online channels. Tracking and monitoring social media and outreach activities, including generating reports. Providing website support including liaising with website users regarding usability feedback, creating and editing web pages, and verifying content is up-to-date. Supports social media strategies by creating and maintaining presence on social media platforms and advising on social media trends and platforms to enhance digital communication strategies. Conducting photography and/or videography shoots for a variety of projects. Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in Communications or Marketing or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum four years of experience in digital communications, content creation, or marketing. Experience producing visual, promotional, and outreach materials for print and digital platforms. Knowledge and experience managing social media channels, including building active engagement, maintaining a consistent voice and expanding reach. Proficiency with social media platforms such as LinkedIn and Meta platforms, scheduling software (e.g. Buffer, Sprout) and web content management tools (Wordpress). Proficiency with Microsoft 365 applications, Adobe Photoshop, and Canva. Strong planning, project management skills with excellent prioritization and time management skills to meet multiple and conflicting deadlines. Demonstrated ability to work independently, showing initiative and good judgment, and be an effective team member. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills (both verbal and written) with the ability to concisely summarize information. Client-services oriented with demonstrated listening and critical thinking skills. Creative and solutions-oriented with exceptional attention to detail and willingness to learn new skills. Assets(Nonessential): Experience using Adobe Premiere. To be successful in this role you will be: Accountable Adaptable Articulate Communicator Cooperative Organized Problem solver Closing Date: 10/19/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 09 -- $70,633 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $90,329. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Communication/Media/Public Relations Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Marketing Communications, Photography, Communications, PR, Project Manager, Marketing, Creative, Technology Apply now » Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
