      "description": "Graduate Program Coordinator Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Graduate Program Coordinator Date Posted: 10/05/2026 Req ID: 50423 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Kinesiology & Physical Education Department: Faculty of Kinesiology & Physical Education Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00019187 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The University of Toronto’s Faculty of Kinesiology and Physical Education is globally recognized for developing and advancing knowledge about the interactions of physical activity and health through outstanding undergraduate and graduate education programs, cutting-edge research and the delivery of sport, recreation and high performance athletic opportunities for students, staff, faculty and community members across the three campuses. In achieving this vision, the Faculty is guided by values of integrity, respect, equity and diversity https://kpe.utoronto.ca/. Your opportunity: The Registrar's Office staff are committed to strong service excellence in supporting the academic and registrarial needs of current undergraduate, graduate and professional master’s students. These services include advising and administration as it relates to registration, financial need, scholarships & awards, and graduation.In addition, the Registrar’s Office is responsible for recruitment and admissions of prospective students, administration of experiential learning opportunities (international, research, in-field learning courses), scheduling of academic courses and exams and providing faculty support. The staff in the Office work collectively toward enhancing the student experience while being committed to operating under principles of equity, diversity and inclusion. The Graduate Program Coordinator is an integral member of a team of administrative and student services professionals who work together to provide exceptional student services in the Faculty of Kinesiology & Physical Education. Reporting to the Assistant Registrar, Graduate Programs, the Graduate Program Coordinator provides day to day program support by answering inquiries from students regarding admission requirements, exam and defence administration, program and tuition information, and funding. The incumbent is responsible for providing support to all KPE graduate students through their programs, ensuring that all Faculty and School of Graduate Studies requirements are met. The Graduate Program Coordinator plays a supporting function for graduate awards processes and competitions, graduate student funding, student registration, petitions & appeals, programs of study, project/thesis requirements, overall degree requirements and eligibility to graduate. Working in collaboration with other members of the Registrar’s Office, the coordinator participates in recruitment initiatives as needed, to attract the best possible candidates for the program. The incumbent will participate in department and Faculty special events which enhance the graduate student experience. Your responsibilities will include: Advising students on academic and/or financial matters by providing options and consequences incorporating personal circumstances impacting academic success and an understanding of an individual's background Assessing and selecting qualified applicants, including exceptional cases Providing detailed information regarding admission requirements to prospective students and applicants Analyzing statistical information to inform admissions projections and planning activities Providing detailed explanations of admissions decisions Promoting programs at recruitment events Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum of four years of experience in an academic student services environment in a university setting at the graduate studies level working with graduate students and graduate programs, including advising on academic matters, funding opportunities, university regulations, and program requirements Experience dealing with with a diverse multicultural pool of students and students in crisis Strong organizational and time-management skills Ability to multi-task while adhering to strict timelines Strong problem-solving skills; high level accuracy and attention to detail Excellent communication (written and oral); excellent interpersonal and advising skills Excellent database management skills Demonstrated computer skills, including advanced skills in Word, Excel, Access, PowerPoint, and Content Management. Assets (Nonessential): Experience with complex funding Excel spreadsheets an asset To be successful in this role you will be: Accountable Diplomatic Proactive Procedural Resourceful Team player Closing Date: 10/19/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 12 -- $84,564 with an annual step progression to a maximum of $108,145. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Registrarial Services Divisional HR Office Email: Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Event Planning, Program Manager, Equity, Database, Hospitality, Management, Finance, Research, Technology Apply now » Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
