    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Office-&-Correspondence-Coordinator-ON/606768717/": {
      "title": "Office & Correspondence Coordinator",
      "description": "Office & Correspondence Coordinator Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Office & Correspondence Coordinator Date Posted: 10/07/2026 Req ID: 50447 Faculty/Division: Office of the President Department: Office of the President Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: Position Summary Under the direction of the Office Manager & Executive Assistant to the President, the Office & Correspondence Coordinator serves as the primary coordinator for the day-to-day administrative operations of the President's Office, ensuring efficient office administration, timely and professional correspondence processes, and seamless logistical support. As Office Coordinator, the incumbent provides general support to help with the smooth running of the President’s Office, including reception duties. These tasks include greeting all visitors and callers to the Office of the President and assisting with their questions and concerns; anticipating, welcoming, and offering refreshments to guests of the President’s Office; and receiving and processing all deliveries to the President’s Office. The incumbent also provides general administrative support to the Officer Manager & Executive Assistant to the President, to the Manager, Correspondence Unit, and to other President’s Office team members as needed. As Correspondence Coordinator, the incumbent supports the monitoring, coordinating, and responding to a heavy volume of correspondence sent to the President for action and disposition. The incumbent serves as a point of contact in receiving and acting upon email and mail, documents, and files for the President’s attention. They are responsible for coding and tracking activity in the University's CRM database (Arbor) and generating reports. The Office & Correspondence Coordinator works in an environment that requires a high degree of sensitivity, situational awareness, responsiveness, independent judgement, and a need to maintain absolute confidentiality. As part of the Office of the President team, the incumbent takes initiative, is proactive in offering support to colleagues, and will troubleshoot issues as they arise. Qualifications Required: Education: Post-secondary degree/diploma or formal business/commercial school training or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience: Minimum five years of progressively responsible experience in a senior administrative position, preferably within a post-secondary or government environment. Demonstrated senior administrative skills within an executive office. Familiarity with the University of Toronto, its policies, procedures and their application strongly preferred. Skills: Must demonstrate strong attention to detail and accuracy. Excellent oral and written communication skills are essential. Proficiency with Outlook (calendar and e-mail), Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Teams. Familiarity with SharePoint is an asset. A willingness to maintain/update knowledge as technology advances. Other: Superior oral and written communication, interpersonal, analytical, decision-making and organizational skills. Demonstrated ability to write clear and concise correspondence. Ability to maintain strict confidentiality. Friendly, with a demonstrated customer-service orientation. Demonstrated initiative, accuracy and meticulous attention to detail. Demonstrated judgment, tact, discretion and ability to handle complex matters of a sensitive and confidential nature. Ability to organize a fluctuating workload in a changing environment. Ability to communicate effectively and professionally with a wide range of individuals across all levels of the University. Ability to work under pressure and to meet deadlines. Ability to work effectively and professionally, both independently and within a team environment. Note: Please submit your résumé along with a one-page cover letter in PDF form. Closing Date: 10/19/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: Admin./Conf. Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: C2 -- Hiring Zone: $67,290 - $86,131 -- Broadband Salary Range: $67,290 - $104,971 Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: CRM, Database, Administrative Assistant, Developer, Sharepoint, Technology, Administrative Apply now » Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance 